// SUBJECT NOTE — Frontier & Philosophy:
//   - Aesthetics: what is beauty? Is it in the object or in us? What is art for? Why does beauty
//     move us so powerfully? Builds on the metaphysics/knowledge threads and pairs naturally
//     after the "ways of knowing" lessons (another kind of value/experience to think clearly about).
//   - HONESTY: the central question (is beauty objective or subjective?) is genuinely open and
//     contested; present the serious positions evenhandedly, none as the winner. Honesty tier 2-3.
//   - PROTECTIVE BACKBONE: taste is heavily MANUFACTURED and MONETIZED. Marketing, status games,
//     hype, and social proof manipulate what we find beautiful/desirable, and people routinely
//     confuse price, brand, scarcity, and status with genuine aesthetic value. The skill: notice
//     when your "taste" is being engineered, separate genuine aesthetic response from manufactured
//     desire, and own your own eye instead of outsourcing it to influencers/markets. Connects to
//     the manipulation-detection spine of the whole band.
//   - EVENHANDED. Em-dashes natural; do NOT run em-dash replacement on Frontier files.
//
// Interaction format: PERSPECTIVES (screen 7). 5 voices. Matches <Perspectives />:
// {id,type,headline,intro,perspectives:[{id,voice,era,stance,quote,argument,evidence,
// strengths_and_limits}],synthesisPrompt,reflectionPrompt}.
//
// QUIZ STANDARD (locked): 8 MC + 1 TF + 1 inference. Short ~1-line options, comparable length,
// plausible misconception distractors, correct rotated/not-longest; teaching in `explanation`.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

